{
  "schema_version": "1.9.2",
  "id": "USN-9200-1",
  "summary": "elfutils vulnerabilities",
  "details": "It was discovered that elfutils incorrectly handled memory when processing\ncertain malformed DWARF data. If a user or automated system were tricked\ninto running readelf on a specially crafted file, an attacker could\npossibly use this issue to cause readelf to crash, resulting in a denial of\nservice, or execute arbitrary code. (CVE-2025-1352)\n\nIt was discovered that strip from elfutils could be made to dereference\ninvalid memory when processing certain sections without data. If a user or\nautomated system were tricked into running strip on a specially crafted\nfile, an attacker could possibly use this issue to cause strip to crash,\nresulting in a denial of service. (CVE-2025-1376)",
